{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity","id":858922,"title":"[Mystery] Supernal is \u2018growing\u2019 with humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-04T05:53:11-07:00","id":858922,"title":"[Mystery] Supernal is \u2018growing\u2019 with humanity","content":"Another topic for talking about one of large Mysteries of setting that can span entire chronicle. This time stuff from historical <b>Dark Eras</b>. Like sourcebook shows in different time periods, what would be called by Diamond and Seers as Supernal looked various over the centuries. At 5000 years BCE what would be latter Pandemonium was great, sunless Forest with burning stone in the middle. At the time of Alexander the Great, circa 300 BCE, same realm looked more like long caverns of labyrinthine geometry and some \u2018shades\u2019 in it. In modern Era we have classical imagery of Pandemonium with Watchtower of Iron Gauntlet inside it. Clearly \u2018Supernal\u2019 is evolving, only Diamond think more that humanity is reflecting this than looking over greater picture. Or that Stygia, like Underworld, was first needed to \u2018dry\u2019 so we could see crypts and catacombs in it.<br /> <br /> <b>What are your answers to this phenomena</b>? My take is that Supernal are \u2018evolving\u2019, just as humanity with it. More humans makes more abstract theories and terms \u2013 just see development of Science in our civilization \u2013 so Supernal Realms are reflecting more and more concepts. <b>That means that Arcana are changing!</b> More things are connected to Supernal, more laws are made there, so more Arcana are reflecting those laws!<br /> <br /> <b>That means that Supernal is connected with Astral, that is reflecting now state of human unconsciousness! </b>Simple humans could not invented what we invented, and so their Supernal was much more simple.<br /> <br /> It also means that Mysterium is right \u2013 <b>Magic ( as Supernal ) is living being and is changing! </b><br /> <br /> Also, this means we need Middle Ages <b>Mage</b> Era \u2013 there we will probably see the first parts of Watchtowers, rising from Supernal up and up with each passing century. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:56:32-07:00","id":858927,"title":"","content":"*deleting this post to make a better one*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-04-2016, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T05:57:16-07:00","id":858929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity#post858922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also means that Mysterium is right \u2013 <b>Magic ( as Supernal ) is living being and is changing! </b></div> </div> </div> </div>OR it means the the Free Council is right, and what happens in the world directs the Supernal! <br /> Probably both. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:03:39-07:00","id":858931,"title":"","content":"Mysterium: Magic is alive and the Supernal is growing and evolving over time<br /> <br /> Free Council: the Supernal changes in reflection of the Phenomenal World. Humanity is in the driver's seat<br /> <br /> Guardians: The Oracles reveal what we need to see in any given age<br /> <br /> Silver Ladder: We are progressing in our discovery of the Supernal, which itself may be largely static, but each generation of the Awakened has progressed closer and closer to the Watchtowers<br /> <br /> [not sure on Adamantine Arrow]<br /> <br /> I'm not sure who: The human mind filters the symbols it can grasp. As society changes, so does the PERCEPTION of the Supernal, but not necessarily the Supernal itself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-04-2016, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:22:42-07:00","id":858944,"title":"","content":"I've always thought of it as a symbiotic relationship between the Supernal and Phenomenal Realms, kind of like how the Exarchs are symbols of Tyranny in the Supernal, but to maintain that state, they have to ensure there are still people to lord over (among other things at least).<br /> <br /> With the 2E change of Prime also having the purview of Truth, and the effects of the 13 Common Practices, it is much more subjective or human-centric since the Principle isn't something we humans, even mages can comprehend, we still have to view it through human understanding, kind of like how you need to form a Lustrum to safely experience the Supernal Realms in 1E.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say it is changing but more of how we are getting a more refined view of the Supernal and the Principal Truth behind it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there is One Truth or Myriad Truths, but the meanings people derive from it is what should ultimately count for Mage the Awakening","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11537-veloranz","name":"Veloranz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:41:37-07:00","id":858956,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call the difference in what Mages see between then and now more refined. It's just different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T07:03:26-07:00","id":858971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=858956#post858956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call the difference in what Mages see between then and now more refined. It's just different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point!<br /> <br /> Maybe its less refined than it is burdened?<br /> <br /> Since it looks like what Mages see looks to be &quot;burdened&quot; with cultural expectations or current realities, which can get weird at times. But Sleepers also contribute to this change, or is it the other way around and just the Supernal Realm affecting us in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11537-veloranz","name":"Veloranz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T07:29:47-07:00","id":858986,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't call it burdened either. It's just different. The Fallen world (I doubt it's just humans, though humans certainly contribute a lot) affects the Supernal and the Supernal affects the Fallen. Humanity's symbols and culture have changed over time and so we see the Supernal differently, and the changes the Fallen has wrought on the Supernal also changed the symbols we see in the Supernal. The Supernal isn't more or less, burdened or refined, etc., it's just different than it was.<br /> <br /> Btw, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> of course the Mysterium is right about magic being alive. All of the books have been written with hints that the various Orders have gotten some things right, so it's really not a surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:14:52-07:00","id":859012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=858931#post858931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure who: The human mind filters the symbols it can grasp. As society changes, so does the PERCEPTION of the Supernal, but not necessarily the Supernal itself</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my preferred explanation. Mages never really see the supernal itself, they see the supernal symbols that underly everything, filtered through the lens of their Path, their Arcana, and their culture. Different cultures associate different symbols with different concepts, so while it makes sense for modern mages to associate power with signs of monarchal rule like crowns, scepters, and thrones, or with biblical figures of power like angels, those symbols wouldn't make any sense at all to a Mage from a culture that predates the bible and has no concept of monarchy. Those Mages would see different symbols in the Aether, that represent power in a way that resonates with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:23:13-07:00","id":859018,"title":"","content":"I personally like the combination of all of these together. If I had to pick one and make it &quot;THE&quot; answer that cruelly murders it's siblings, it would be Free Council's interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:26:44-07:00","id":859022,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the supernal doesn't really look like what mages see through mage sight. It doesn't look like <i>anything.</i> There are just raw symbols. Metaphorical representations are a filter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:36:52-07:00","id":859029,"title":"","content":"I would say that the changes partly represent changing perspectives, that is, people over time associate with a bit different symbols of an Arcanum than they did in times past. But as Awakenings tend to differ in relative amount of suffering they put people through even in a single era and as every mage in our era still gets only one dot of Resolve/Composure and Neolithic mages got two dots, I think that the Watchtowers are indeed becoming more refined. They are attuning mages to the Supernal realms better and better. Who knows where will that lead in the future - maybe one day there will not be any resistance from the Supernal at all...<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Resistance Attribute:</b> The divine ember of enlightenment burns those who would seize it with far fiercer flame than the Awakenings of later millennia, and the very process of opening the soul to the Supernal leaves only the hardiest sane and alive. Neolithic Awakened begin with two bonus dots in Resistance Attributes rather than just one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 04-04-2016, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:53:57-07:00","id":859116,"title":"","content":"I don't know, and it's not really an issue I need an answer to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T11:18:45-07:00","id":859132,"title":"","content":"Other thing that come to from point of thinking about Watchtowers - <b>What if they &quot;seeded&quot; by Oracles (?) to recreate Celestial Ladder in each Realm?</b> And that it need MILLENIA to grow in to proper Watchtower? Remember, in Anima Mundi we have The Spire Perilous:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Spire Perilous is a symbol of everything that humanity has squandered. Legends say that this was the axis mundi: the fixed center of existence that the spiritually aware could use to guide their paths. Tomystics and worshipers, the Spire Perilous should be Yggdrasil, Mount Meru, Atziluth of the Tree of Life \u2014 the way to absolute truth, unfettered by human desire. And so it would be, if not for the fact that the Spire itself was fettered to Awakened will long ago \u2014 and broke under the strain. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-04-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:27:29-07:00","id":859165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=859132#post859132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other thing that come to from point of thinking about Watchtowers - <b>What if they &quot;seeded&quot; by Oracles (?) to recreate Celestial Ladder in each Realm?</b> And that it need MILLENIA to grow in to proper Watchtower? Remember, in Anima Mundi we have The Spire Perilous:</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll need to unpack what you mean by the reference to the Spire Perilous (I can think of some things you might mean, but it's not obvious).<br /> <br /> That said, that's actually a pretty neat idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T19:21:12-07:00","id":859392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=859165#post859165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll need to unpack what you mean by the reference to the Spire Perilous (I can think of some things you might mean, but it's not obvious).<br /> <br /> That said, that's actually a pretty neat idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>To travel to the Dreamtime layer of the Astral beyond the Omphalos stone, there are two ways to go to travel to reach the Dreamtime (the dreaming soul of the world): <b>The Spire Perilous</b>, which is the remenants of the Fall that devastated reality and the representation of humanity's enlightenment reaching out to the universe, and <b>The Swath of Destruction</b>, which is the representation of humanity's impact on the world and it's environment.<br /> <br /> For some reason, many groups refuse to even see the Swath of Destruction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I wonder why...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T20:02:29-07:00","id":859410,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Michael has a point, what the heck does Wyrd mean by referencing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T00:57:28-07:00","id":859519,"title":"","content":"Or maybe the Watchtowers are eating the souls of mages who sign their names on them and the symbology is the product of the developing oracle-gestalt. They were said to be rather different from other supernal realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T01:30:51-07:00","id":859523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=859410#post859410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Michael has a point, what the heck does Wyrd mean by referencing it?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Spire Perilous</b> is direct Astral representation of what is left of Celestial Ladder ( or so is theory on it ) - in that it was not &quot;ladder&quot; but Spire. Like mythological Atlantis Ocean Spire. And now Watchtowers are also &quot;spires&quot; - they are Tower so the look like Spire. What if the Spire is needed to connect humans souls to it. <b>And so Watchtowers are Supernal different &quot;peaks&quot; of Spire Perilous, rising with each generation after the Fall to rebuild it?</b><br /> <br /> In nutshell - <b>What if Watchtowers are new Celestial Ladders for human souls? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-05-2016, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T02:26:41-07:00","id":859529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=859523#post859523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Spire Perilous</b> is direct Astral representation of what is left of Celestial Ladder ( or so is theory on it ) - in that it was not &quot;ladder&quot; but Spire. Like mythological Atlantis Ocean Spire. And now Watchtowers are also &quot;spires&quot; - they are Tower so the look like Spire. What if the Spire is needed to connect humans souls to it. <b>And so Watchtowers are Supernal different &quot;peaks&quot; of Spire Perilous, rising with each generation after the Fall to rebuild it?</b><br /> <br /> In nutshell - <b>What if Watchtowers are new Celestial Ladders for human souls? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </b></div> </div> </div> </div>They could be of a sort, although not quite there yet (if they are still &quot;growing&quot; as it were) or perhaps in a post-Exarch world, the recreation of the Celestial Ladder (Ascension for everybody) is no longer possible and what they are serve as now are as beacons for as many human souls as possible / receptive to the truths that each Watchtower represents?<br /> <br /> A theory of cycles between the rise and fall of various &quot;Spires&quot; is interesting, like how each Spire represents the state of humanity in that period and can only be sustained while they are relevant, which then crumble to make way for new Spires to rise.<br /> <br /> This reminds me of the cycles that the world of Dark Souls has if you guys know of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11537-veloranz","name":"Veloranz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:18:00-07:00","id":920942,"title":"","content":"More on the topics Mystery - just see new <b>Kurzgesagt \u2013 In a Nutshell </b>clip...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dGiQaabX3_o\" data-code=\"dGiQaabX3_o\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dGiQaabX3_o/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> So some new questions on Mystery:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would other Homo species have their own Awakened in past?</li> <li>WHEN would first Awakened of Homo Sapiens first emerged - 50 000 years ago? 10 000 years ago? At 7 500 years ago starts <i>Sundered World</i> Dark Era and clearly Awakened - beside their modern society - works more or less like modern mages ( from magic-mechanics stand point, like anatomically we are the same with first Homo Sapiens ).</li> <li>When first idea of 'Atlantis' ( as Times Before ) would be made? Maybe 'Atlantis' was first created by OTHER Homo species?</li> </ol>To counter those reflections, I point to my own <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy\">Children of Stars Legacy</a></b> that has totally different take on the matter... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-25-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:17:18-07:00","id":921443,"title":"","content":"Astral Realms implies that at least neaderthals could have awakened. Neanderthals were certainly encompassed by the Temenos and to have had access to the Wellspring.<br /> <br /> Although he's goetia in the book, personally, I'd be tempted to make him a neaderthal morphean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T14:37:10-07:00","id":921694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/858922-mystery-supernal-is-\u2018growing\u2019-with-humanity?p=921443#post921443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astral Realms implies that at least neaderthals could have awakened. Neanderthals were certainly encompassed by the Temenos and to have had access to the Wellspring.<br /> <br /> Although he's goetia in the book, personally, I'd be tempted to make him a neaderthal morphean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, especially considering the fact that homo neandertalis is a whole different species in the same genus. I wonder if that means other hominids could Awaken as well. Certainly, I would expect other subspecies of homo sapiens to have been able to when they were around, in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T14:53:09-07:00","id":921702,"title":"","content":"Actually, giving it a little more thought, it's possible the Last Neaderthal is meant to be humanity's memory of neanderthals. So it's less definite than I suggested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T14:57:14-07:00","id":921704,"title":"","content":"Whenever a Mage reaches into the world and replaces it with their Supernally-charged Imago, the Supernal takes whatever was replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:08:23-08:00","id":1006291,"title":"","content":"More ideas to throw on evolution of magic - <b>What if mages are separate human race altogether that mix with normal humanity?</b> Here is example from <b>Madame Xanadu</b> comics series. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/FhRTa\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div clas